---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import NewsletterEmbed from '../../components/NewsletterEmbed.astro';

const contactHref = `mailto:hi@maxguerois.com?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Your article on life after leaving a startup')}&body=${encodeURIComponent("Hi Max,\r\n\r\nI loved your article about life after leaving a startup.\r\n\r\nHere's my experience:\r\n\r\n")}`;
---
<ArticleLayout
    title="Life after leaving my startup: Max Guerois"
    description="What leaving Lucis felt like, and the struggles that kept coming up in conversations with 50+ founders."
    ogUrl="https://maxguerois.com/newsletter/post-exit"
    ogImage="https://maxguerois.com/health-journey/post-exit.webp"
    ogImageAlt="Max lying in the grass beside an outdoor sauna"
    ogImageWidth={1600}
    ogImageHeight={1200}
>
    <div class="container">
        <a href="/newsletter" class="back">← All articles</a>

        <div class="article-meta">October 30, 2026</div>
        <h1 class="article-title">Life after leaving my startup</h1>

        <img
            class="article-img"
            src="/health-journey/post-exit.webp"
            alt="Max lying in the grass beside an outdoor sauna"
            width="1600"
            height="1200"
            fetchpriority="high"
            decoding="async"
        >

        <div class="article-body">
            <p>Nobody talks about post-exit life. So here's my story.</p>

            <p>I've spoken with 50+ founders who sold their businesses or left their companies, sometimes by choice, sometimes pushed out.</p>

            <p>The same struggles kept coming up.</p>

            <p>For me, the weirdest period of my life came after I left Lucis, my first startup.</p>

            <p>I'll be honest: it hit me hard.</p>

            <ul class="post-exit-points">
                <li>Losing your identity and motivation.</li>
                <li>Feeling worthless without the company.</li>
                <li>Pressure to build something new.</li>
                <li>Wondering: do I actually want this, or do I just need to prove I can build again?</li>
            </ul>

            <p>That last one is really, really hard.</p>

            <p>Many founders won't say this publicly, for fear of complaining about “champagne problems” or sounding ungrateful.</p>

            <p>Travel was great for a while. Then I started feeling useless and guilty.</p>

            <p>I love a sauna reset. Taking care of my health helped, too.</p>

            <p>But none of that, on its own, gave me back a sense of purpose.</p>

            <p>Then comes introspection. It helps, but you can spend so long analysing yourself that you stop doing anything.</p>

            <p>I'll never forget that period.</p>

            <p>I'm curious how other founders felt after getting acquired, selling their business, or leaving their company.</p>

            <p>Tell me your story at <a class="post-exit-contact" href={contactHref}>hi@maxguerois.com</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="article-footer">
            <span class="author-line">By <a href="/">Max Guerois</a></span>
        </div>

        <div class="post-exit-subscribe">
            <NewsletterEmbed />
        </div>
    </div>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
    .article-img { height: auto; }
    .post-exit-points {
        padding-left: var(--sp-6);
        margin: 0 0 var(--sp-6);
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        line-height: 1.75;
    }
    .post-exit-points li + li { margin-top: var(--sp-2); }
    .post-exit-contact {
        color: var(--text);
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
    .post-exit-contact:hover { color: var(--accent); }
    .post-exit-subscribe { margin-top: var(--sp-12); }
</style>
